<decision #track.verify-eidolon-resource-native-app-lifecycle.real-provider apiVersion="codument.tech/v1alpha1" { priority = "P0" status = "accepted" durable_candidate = true } (
  <question ?01M0QPC3W6FS2X1VCHA5B0RDA4>
  What proves the terminal lifecycle is usable?
  </?01M0QPC3W6FS2X1VCHA5B0RDA4>
  <answer (
    <raw-answer ?01M0QPC3W6FS2X1VCHA5B0RDA5>
    A fresh journey through the current compiled product and current provider preset.
    </?01M0QPC3W6FS2X1VCHA5B0RDA5>
    <decision-text ?01M0QPC3W6FS2X1VCHA5B0RDA6>
    The terminal acceptance SHALL use compiled eidolon workflow agent without a model override; deterministic providers may reproduce boundaries but cannot replace the final journey.
    </?01M0QPC3W6FS2X1VCHA5B0RDA6>
    <rationale ?01M0QPC3W6FS2X1VCHA5B0RDA7>
    The reported failure concerned real provider latency and tool payload behavior.
    </?01M0QPC3W6FS2X1VCHA5B0RDA7>
    <evidence ?01M0QPC3W6FS2X1VCHA5B0RDA8>
    The mission preserves the prior 142.956-second and invalid_tool_call_payload incident facts; the ephemeral original sessions no longer exist.
    </?01M0QPC3W6FS2X1VCHA5B0RDA8>
  )>
  <confidence ?01M0QPC3W6FS2X1VCHA5B0RDA9>
  0.99
  </?01M0QPC3W6FS2X1VCHA5B0RDA9>
  <reversibility ?01M0QPC3W6FS2X1VCHA5B0RDAA>
  moderate
  </?01M0QPC3W6FS2X1VCHA5B0RDAA>
)>

<decision #track.verify-eidolon-resource-native-app-lifecycle.isolation apiVersion="codument.tech/v1alpha1" { priority = "P0" status = "accepted" durable_candidate = true } (
  <question ?01M0QPC3W6FS2X1VCHA5B0RDAB>
  How can the real provider be used without modifying user state?
  </?01M0QPC3W6FS2X1VCHA5B0RDAB>
  <answer (
    <raw-answer ?01M0QPC3W6FS2X1VCHA5B0RDAC>
    Run with mktemp HOME/global/workspace and copy only the two current provider configuration files into the temporary HOME.
    </?01M0QPC3W6FS2X1VCHA5B0RDAC>
    <decision-text ?01M0QPC3W6FS2X1VCHA5B0RDAD>
    The harness SHALL initialize and mutate only isolated roots, redact credentials from all durable evidence, and leave the real ~/.eidolon untouched.
    </?01M0QPC3W6FS2X1VCHA5B0RDAD>
    <rationale ?01M0QPC3W6FS2X1VCHA5B0RDAE>
    Provider configuration is required for realism; user assets and secrets are not acceptance outputs.
    </?01M0QPC3W6FS2X1VCHA5B0RDAE>
    <evidence ?01M0QPC3W6FS2X1VCHA5B0RDAF>
    Local config resolution supports project-or-HOME `.eidolon/llm-provider.json` and `agent-present.json`, while global init accepts an explicit root.
    </?01M0QPC3W6FS2X1VCHA5B0RDAF>
  )>
  <confidence ?01M0QPC3W6FS2X1VCHA5B0RDAG>
  0.98
  </?01M0QPC3W6FS2X1VCHA5B0RDAG>
  <reversibility ?01M0QPC3W6FS2X1VCHA5B0RDAH>
  high
  </?01M0QPC3W6FS2X1VCHA5B0RDAH>
)>

<decision #track.verify-eidolon-resource-native-app-lifecycle.authorization apiVersion="codument.tech/v1alpha1" { priority = "P0" status = "accepted" durable_candidate = true } (
  <question ?01M0QPC3W6FS2X1VCHA5B0RDAJ>
  How are publication and execution separated?
  </?01M0QPC3W6FS2X1VCHA5B0RDAJ>
  <answer (
    <raw-answer ?01M0QPC3W6FS2X1VCHA5B0RDAK>
    Three explicit turns in one durable session.
    </?01M0QPC3W6FS2X1VCHA5B0RDAK>
    <decision-text ?01M0QPC3W6FS2X1VCHA5B0RDAM>
    Create SHALL not publish or run; the second turn SHALL authorize publication only; the third SHALL authorize execution and bind input.
    </?01M0QPC3W6FS2X1VCHA5B0RDAM>
    <rationale ?01M0QPC3W6FS2X1VCHA5B0RDAN>
    Proof, publication authorization and execution authorization are separate product facts.
    </?01M0QPC3W6FS2X1VCHA5B0RDAN>
    <evidence ?01M0QPC3W6FS2X1VCHA5B0RDAP>
    Existing workflow CLI and native tools expose separate authoring, publication, instance and run transitions.
    </?01M0QPC3W6FS2X1VCHA5B0RDAP>
  )>
  <confidence ?01M0QPC3W6FS2X1VCHA5B0RDAQ>
  0.99
  </?01M0QPC3W6FS2X1VCHA5B0RDAQ>
  <reversibility ?01M0QPC3W6FS2X1VCHA5B0RDAR>
  low
  </?01M0QPC3W6FS2X1VCHA5B0RDAR>
)>

<decision #track.verify-eidolon-resource-native-app-lifecycle.fact-driven-repair apiVersion="codument.tech/v1alpha1" { priority = "P0" status = "accepted" durable_candidate = true } (
  <question ?01M0QPC3W6FS2X1VCHA5B0RDAS>
  How may a failed journey be repaired?
  </?01M0QPC3W6FS2X1VCHA5B0RDAS>
  <answer (
    <raw-answer ?01M0QPC3W6FS2X1VCHA5B0RDAT>
    Only from stable provider/tool/runtime facts in the owning generic component.
    </?01M0QPC3W6FS2X1VCHA5B0RDAT>
    <decision-text ?01M0QPC3W6FS2X1VCHA5B0RDAV>
    No repair may add natural-language, node-name, App/workflow-name or alias heuristics, nor a workflow-specific actor/session/compactor/resource authority.
    </?01M0QPC3W6FS2X1VCHA5B0RDAV>
    <rationale ?01M0QPC3W6FS2X1VCHA5B0RDAW>
    Model-owned semantics and deterministic structured components are a non-negotiable architecture boundary.
    </?01M0QPC3W6FS2X1VCHA5B0RDAW>
    <evidence ?01M0QPC3W6FS2X1VCHA5B0RDAX>
    The mission and completed architecture tracks explicitly prohibit fuzzy host routing and parallel authorities.
    </?01M0QPC3W6FS2X1VCHA5B0RDAX>
  )>
  <confidence ?01M0QPC3W6FS2X1VCHA5B0RDAY>
  1.0
  </?01M0QPC3W6FS2X1VCHA5B0RDAY>
  <reversibility ?01M0QPC3W6FS2X1VCHA5B0RDAZ>
  low
  </?01M0QPC3W6FS2X1VCHA5B0RDAZ>
)>
